From 111abac8b92bce58b7fee7c9cc80a4e1498fe3c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:15:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dmaengine: qcom: bam_dma: synchronize channel callbacks

BAM implements termination but has no device_synchronize callback.
Terminating a channel removes queued descriptors and resets an active
pipe, but a virt-dma completion tasklet may already have detached its
completed list and be running a client callback. dmaengine_synchronize()
and dmaengine_terminate_sync() consequently return without waiting for
that callback, contrary to their lifetime guarantee.

Implement device_synchronize with vchan_synchronize() on the selected
channel. Drain that channel's completion tasklet outside its spinlock;
leave other channels and the device's shared issue tasklet alone. Keep
the existing cancellation, descriptor ownership and hardware reset paths.
Clients must still stop the attached engine and prevent new submissions
as required by the DMA API. This does not fix client resubmission or
master/transfer teardown ordering.

A host model executes eight exact driver/virt-dma/DMA API callbacks and
the two relevant probe assignments. It passes 256 cases/3,328 checks,
compared with 536 pre-change failures, and rejects eight regression
controls. It covers both channel selections, combined and split APIs,
active callbacks, queued descriptors and an unrelated active channel.
Six native ARM/ARM64 objects build with LLVM21, W=1 and strict callback
diagnostics without warnings or errors.

Tasklets, callbacks, lists, hardware and owner retirement are synthetic;
no real DMA, stale-memory access, audio or phone operations execute.
Codex generated this fix, model and changelog. Human review and DCO
certification remain pending.

Fixes: e7c0fe2a5c84 ("dmaengine: add Qualcomm BAM dma driver")
---
 drivers/dma/qcom/bam_dma.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/dma/qcom/bam_dma.c b/drivers/dma/qcom/bam_dma.c
index f67a93a37..c68c44c35 100644
--- a/drivers/dma/qcom/bam_dma.c
+++ b/drivers/dma/qcom/bam_dma.c
@@ -784,6 +784,11 @@ static int bam_dma_terminate_all(struct dma_chan *chan)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void bam_dma_synchronize(struct dma_chan *chan)
+{
+	vchan_synchronize(to_virt_chan(chan));
+}
+
 /**
  * bam_pause - Pause DMA channel
  * @chan: dma channel
@@ -1359,6 +1364,7 @@ static int bam_dma_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	bdev->common.device_pause = bam_pause;
 	bdev->common.device_resume = bam_resume;
 	bdev->common.device_terminate_all = bam_dma_terminate_all;
+	bdev->common.device_synchronize = bam_dma_synchronize;
 	bdev->common.device_issue_pending = bam_issue_pending;
 	bdev->common.device_tx_status = bam_tx_status;
 	bdev->common.dev = bdev->dev;
